        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(envelope): accept timestamp 0 in formatEnvelopeTimestamp",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n`formatEnvelopeTimestamp` used `if (!ts)` to check for missing timestamps, which incorrectly rejected the valid numeric timestamp `0` (Unix epoch). Replace the falsy check with an explicit `ts === undefined || ts === null` check.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nIn `src/auto-reply/envelope.ts:117`, `formatEnvelopeTimestamp` guards with `if (!ts) { return undefined; }`. Since `ts` is typed `number | Date | undefined`, the value `0` is a valid millisecond timestamp (representing 1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z), but `!0 === true` causes it to be silently rejected.\n\n**Code evidence**: In `envelope.ts:117`, `!ts` is falsy for `0` (valid Unix epoch timestamp).\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe check `!ts` conflates \"missing/undefined\" with \"falsy numeric value\". For a parameter typed `number | Date | undefined`, the only invalid value is `undefined` (and technically `null`). Using `!` also rejects `0`, which is a valid timestamp.\n\n## Why This Fix\n\nThe minimal fix: change `if (!ts)` → `if (ts === undefined || ts === null)`. This preserves the existing behavior for `undefined` and `Date` instances (always truthy) while correctly accepting `0`.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **Before**: `formatEnvelopeTimestamp(0)` silently returns `undefined` — the Unix epoch timestamp is dropped from envelope formatting.\n- **After**: `formatEnvelopeTimestamp(0)` returns `\"Thu 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z\"` (in UTC mode).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before**: `formatEnvelopeTimestamp(0)` returns `undefined` → FAIL\n- **After**: `formatEnvelopeTimestamp(0)` returns formatted timestamp → PASS\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Before (on main)\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx proof.mjs\n=== formatEnvelopeTimestamp(0) ===\nFAIL: formatEnvelopeTimestamp(0) returned undefined\n      The valid Unix epoch timestamp is being rejected by the falsy check.\n```\n\n### After (with fix)\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx proof.mjs\n=== formatEnvelopeTimestamp(0) ===\nResult: Thu 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z\nPASS: formatEnvelopeTimestamp(0) correctly formatted the Unix epoch timestamp.\n\n=== formatEnvelopeTimestamp(undefined) ===\nResult: undefined\nPASS: undefined correctly returns undefined.\n```\n\n## Tests and Validation\n\n- `pnpm check` passed (no lint errors)\n- Added 2 regression tests: timestamp 0 is formatted; undefined still returns undefined\n",
